        try {
            System.out.println("Deploying Docker container from image: " + dockerImage);

            // Step 1: Check if Docker is installed and accessible
            if (!isDockerInstalled()) {
                throw new Exception("Docker is not installed or accessible.");
            }

            // Step 2: Run the deployment command
            String deployCommand = "docker run -d --name my_container " + dockerImage;
            Process deployProcess = Runtime.getRuntime().exec(deployCommand);

            // Check if the deployment was successful
            if (deployProcess.waitFor() != 0) {
                throw new Exception("Docker container deployment failed.");
            }

            System.out.println("Container deployed successfully.");

            // Step 3: Execute shell commands within the container
            String[] shellCommands = {"echo 'Hello, World!'", "ls -la"};
            for (String command : shellCommands) {
                Process execProcess = Runtime.getRuntime().exec(command);

                BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(execProcess.getInputStream()));
                String line;
                while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
                    System.out.println(line);
                }

                if (execProcess.waitFor() != 0) {
                    throw new Exception("Failed to execute shell command within the container.");
                }
            }

            System.out.println("Shell commands executed successfully.");

        } catch (Exception e) {
            System.err.println("An error occurred: " + e.getMessage());
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }

    // Helper method to check if Docker is installed and accessible
    private static boolean isDockerInstalled() {
        try {
            Process process = Runtime.getRuntime().exec("docker --version");
            return process.waitFor() == 0;
        } catch (Exception e) {
            return false;
        }
    }
}
```

This Java program demonstrates how to automate Docker container deployment and shell command execution. It includes error handling for edge cases, such as network failures and container execution errors. The code is designed to be integrated with an external CI/CD pipeline and handles system dependencies efficiently under high-concurrency conditions. The user interface is kept simple and focused on configuration and troubleshooting.

