This is a basic example of a Rust program that integrates with an external REST API using the `reqwest` crate to fetch weather data. It uses the Tokio library for handling asynchronous requests. The program accepts a city name as a command line argument and prints out the current temperature.

Please note that you need to replace `"https://api.openweathermap.org/data/2.5/weather?q={}&appid=YOUR_API_KEY"` with the actual API endpoint of the weather service you want to use, and replace `"YOUR_API_KEY"` with your actual API key.

Also, make sure you have `reqwest`, `tokio`, and `serde` dependencies in your `Cargo.toml` file.

